:: StoryTitle
DASH Diet Game

:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "C3D4E5F6-A7B8-4012-9DEF-123456789012",
  "format": "SugarCube",
  "format-version": "2.30.0",
  "start": "Story innit",
  "zoom": 1
}

:: Story innit [Important/Needed] {"position": "100,100", "size": "100,100"}
/*
SYSTEM CODE: runs once at the very start.

Variables:
- $playerName  : player name
- $score       : total correct quiz answers (0 to 6)
- $wrong       : total wrong quiz answers (0 to 6)
- $mealScore   : meal builder running score
- $round       : current quiz round 1 to 6
- $lastFood    : the food just classified
- $lastCorrect : whether the last answer was right
- $meal        : list of ingredients picked

You do not need to edit this.
*/

<<set $playerName to "Explorer">>
<<set $score to 0>>
<<set $wrong to 0>>
<<set $mealScore to 0>>
<<set $round to 1>>
<<set $lastFood to "">>
<<set $lastCorrect to false>>
<<set $meal to []>>
/* Food-pool state (UPDATE6/7/8): seenFoods tracks which pool ids have
   already been shown this play-through; currentFood is the object the
   generic Food Card / Food Result render. Reset here so PLAY AGAIN
   starts from a full, unshuffled-order pool. */
<<set $seenFoods to []>>
<<set $currentFood to null>>
/* Meal-builder random subset: null here so each fresh game (and PLAY
   AGAIN) re-rolls which foods appear in the build-your-own-meal grids. */
<<set $mealPick to null>>
/* Diet choice (everything / vegetarian / vegan). Set on the Diet Choice
   screen right after Welcome. Foods tagged diet:"meat"/"dairy" are hidden
   for the matching diet so no one is shown food they do not eat. */
<<set $playerDiet to "everything">>
/* One-shot guard so Meal Result's submitResponse fires exactly once
   per play-through. Reset on Story innit so PLAY AGAIN gets a fresh
   shot. See ::Meal Result for the submit body. */
<<set $submittedThisSession to false>>

/* DAILY GATE: DASH is a once-per-day quest. localStorage holds the last
   calendar date the participant finished it; if that matches today,
   route to the Already Today screen instead of the quiz. Tomorrow the
   date differs, the gate falls off, and a fresh round is available. */
<<set $dashDone to false>>
<<script>>
State.variables.todayDate = (new Date()).toISOString().slice(0, 10);
try {
  var ua = (typeof navigator !== "undefined" && navigator.userAgent) || "";
  var m = ua.match(/CCQApp\/([^\s]+)/);
  State.variables.currentPid = m ? m[1] : "";
  var sav = window.localStorage.getItem("dash_save");
  if (sav) {
    var s = JSON.parse(sav);
    var samePid = (s.pid || "") === State.variables.currentPid;
    if (samePid && s.dashDate && s.dashDate === State.variables.todayDate) {
      State.variables.dashDone = true;
    }
  }
} catch (e) { /* keep $dashDone false */ }
<</script>>
<<if $dashDone>><<goto "Already Today">><<else>><<goto "Welcome">><</if>>

:: Already Today [Important/Needed nobr] {"position": "100,225", "size": "100,100"}
/*
DAILY GATE SCREEN: shown when the participant already finished DASH
today. Friendly come-back-tomorrow message with a single Home button.
The gate is set in Story innit from the localStorage `dash_save` date
stamp written at the end of Meal Result.
*/

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span></div>
<div class="content">

<span class="hero-emoji">✅</span>

<h1 class="intro-title">All done for today</h1>

<p class="narrative center">You finished today's DASH diet quest. Nice work.</p>

<p class="narrative center">Come back tomorrow for 10 new foods.</p>

<div class="spacer"></div>

<a class="btn-primary ccq-home-trigger" href="javascript:void(0)">BACK TO CARDIOCARE QUEST</a>

</div>
</div>

:: Welcome [Important/Needed nobr] {"position": "225,100", "size": "100,100"}
/*
INCITING MOMENT: Greeting + hook. One button.
Card 1 of 2 before gameplay starts.
*/

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span></div>
<div class="content">

<span class="hero-emoji">🥗</span>

<h1 class="intro-title">DASH Diet Game</h1>

<p class="narrative center">Hey $playerName.</p>

<p class="narrative">DASH is a way of eating that is proven to lower high blood pressure.</p>

<p class="narrative">This game shows you which everyday foods help and which ones work against you.</p>

<div class="spacer"></div>

<a class="btn-primary" data-passage="Diet Choice">NEXT</a>

</div>
</div>

:: Diet Choice [Important/Needed nobr] {"position": "225,225", "size": "100,100"}
/*
DIET CHOICE: Ask once what the player eats. Sets $playerDiet, which
setup.dash.fitsDiet() reads to hide meat/dairy foods for vegetarian /
vegan players in both the quiz and the meal builder.
*/

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span></div>
<div class="content">

<span class="hero-emoji">🍽️</span>

<h2 class="intro-title">What do you eat?</h2>

<p class="narrative center">Pick one. We will only show you foods you actually eat.</p>

<div class="spacer"></div>

<<link '🍗  I eat everything'>><<set $playerDiet to "everything">><<goto "How To Play">><</link>>

<<link '🥗  Vegetarian (no meat)'>><<set $playerDiet to "vegetarian">><<goto "How To Play">><</link>>

<<link '🌱  Vegan (no meat or dairy)'>><<set $playerDiet to "vegan">><<goto "How To Play">><</link>>

</div>
</div>

<<script>>
setTimeout(function () {
  var links = document.querySelectorAll('.content a.macro-link, .content a.link-internal');
  for (var i = 0; i < links.length; i++) {
    links[i].classList.add('btn-primary');
    links[i].style.marginBottom = '12px';
  }
}, 0);
<</script>>

:: How To Play [Important/Needed nobr] {"position": "350,100", "size": "100,100"}
/*
RULES in one screen.
Card 2 of 2 before gameplay starts.
*/

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span></div>
<div class="content">

<span class="hero-emoji">🍎</span>

<h2 class="intro-title">Two Parts</h2>

<p class="narrative"><strong>Part 1:</strong> Six food cards. Tap whether each food lowers or raises blood pressure. Learn why.</p>

<p class="narrative"><strong>Part 2:</strong> Build a meal. Pick ingredients. See what they do together.</p>

<p class="narrative">Right or wrong, you leave knowing more than you came with.</p>

<div class="spacer"></div>

<a class="btn-primary" data-passage="Round Start">START ROUND 1</a>

</div>
</div>

:: Round Start [Important/Needed nobr] {"position": "475,100", "size": "100,100"}
/*
ROUND ROUTER (UPDATE6/7/8).
No longer a UI screen. Draws the next food from the weighted,
non-repeating pool via setup.dash.pickFood(). When the pool is
exhausted pickFood() returns null and we advance to the meal builder
(the same phase the old Food Result advanced to after the last card).
Otherwise we render the single generic Food Card for $currentFood.
*/
<<set _f to setup.dash.pickFood()>>
<<if _f is null>><<goto "Meal Builder Intro">><<else>><<goto "Food Card">><</if>>

:: Food Card [Important/Needed nobr] {"position": "600,100", "size": "100,100"}
/*
GENERIC FOOD CARD (UPDATE6/7/8).
Renders whatever setup.dash.pickFood() stashed in $currentFood. The two
choices score against $currentFood.correct: a matching answer bumps
$score and sets $lastCorrect true; a mismatch bumps $wrong and sets it
false. Then on to Food Result. Replaces the old hardcoded Food Card 1..6.
*/

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span><span class="round-label">Round $round of <<print setup.dash.eligibleCount()>></span></div>

<div class="meters-wrap">
<div class="meter-row"><div class="meter-label">Correct</div><div class="meter-bar"><div class="meter-bar-fill correct" @style="'width: ' + Math.min(100, ($score / 6) * 100) + '%'"></div></div></div>
<div class="meter-row"><div class="meter-label">Wrong</div><div class="meter-bar"><div class="meter-bar-fill wrong" @style="'width: ' + Math.min(100, ($wrong / 6) * 100) + '%'"></div></div></div>
</div>

<div class="content">

<div class="quiz-card">
<span class="quiz-emoji"><<print $currentFood.emoji>></span>
<h2 class="quiz-name"><<print $currentFood.name>></h2>
<p class="quiz-desc"><<print $currentFood.desc>></p>
</div>

<div class="question-prompt">What does it do to blood pressure?</div>

<div class="choice-row">

<<link '<span>LOWERS BP</span>'>>
<<set $lastFood to $currentFood.id>>
<<if $currentFood.correct is "lowers">>
<<set $lastCorrect to true>>
<<set $score to $score + 1>>
<<else>>
<<set $lastCorrect to false>>
<<set $wrong to $wrong + 1>>
<</if>>
<<goto "Food Result">>
<</link>>

<<link '<span>RAISES BP</span>'>>
<<set $lastFood to $currentFood.id>>
<<if $currentFood.correct is "raises">>
<<set $lastCorrect to true>>
<<set $score to $score + 1>>
<<else>>
<<set $lastCorrect to false>>
<<set $wrong to $wrong + 1>>
<</if>>
<<goto "Food Result">>
<</link>>

</div>
</div>
</div>

<<script>>
setTimeout(function () {
  var btns = document.querySelectorAll('.choice-row a.macro-link, .choice-row a.link-internal');
  if (btns.length >= 1) btns[0].classList.add('choice-btn', 'lowers');
  if (btns.length >= 2) btns[1].classList.add('choice-btn', 'raises');
}, 0);
<</script>>

:: Food Result [Important/Needed nobr] {"position": "725,100", "size": "100,100"}
/*
RESULT OF EACH FOOD CARD.
Tells the player whether they were right and explains why.
Moves to next round or meal builder after round 6.
*/

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span><span class="round-label">Round $round of <<print setup.dash.eligibleCount()>></span></div>

<div class="meters-wrap">
<div class="meter-row"><div class="meter-label">Correct</div><div class="meter-bar"><div class="meter-bar-fill correct" @style="'width: ' + Math.min(100, ($score / 6) * 100) + '%'"></div></div></div>
<div class="meter-row"><div class="meter-label">Wrong</div><div class="meter-bar"><div class="meter-bar-fill wrong" @style="'width: ' + Math.min(100, ($wrong / 6) * 100) + '%'"></div></div></div>
</div>

<div class="content">

<div class="result-card">
<span class="result-emoji"><<print $currentFood.emoji>></span>

<<if $lastCorrect is true>><div class="result-verdict correct">Correct</div><<else>><div class="result-verdict wrong">Not quite</div><</if>>

<p class="result-explain"><<print $currentFood.explain>></p>
</div>

<!-- Termination is decided by the pool, not by $round: Round Start's
     pickFood() returns null once every food has been seen and routes to
     Meal Builder Intro. So Food Result always just advances the round
     counter and hands back to Round Start for the next draw.
     Per-round "BACK TO CARDIOCAREQUEST" stays removed — the burger
     menu (≡) already exposes "Go to dashboard" on every screen. -->
<<set $round to $round + 1>>
<a class="btn-primary" data-passage="Round Start">NEXT FOOD</a>

</div>
</div>

:: Meal Builder Intro [Important/Needed nobr] {"position": "850,100", "size": "100,100"}
/*
TRANSITION: Cards done. Introduce meal building.
*/

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span><span class="round-label">Part 2</span></div>
<div class="content">

<span class="hero-emoji">🍽️</span>

<h2 class="intro-title">Build a Meal</h2>

<p class="narrative center">You scored $score out of <<print setup.dash.eligibleCount()>> on the cards.</p>

<p class="narrative">Now pick ingredients to build a meal. Tap each one to add it. The score bar fills as you choose.</p>

<p class="narrative">No wrong answers here. The point is to see what each choice does.</p>

<div class="spacer"></div>

<a class="btn-primary" data-passage="Meal Builder">START BUILDING</a>

</div>
</div>

:: Meal Builder [Important/Needed nobr] {"position": "975,100", "size": "100,100"}
/*
MEAL BUILDER: Player picks ingredients.
Each <<linkreplace>> can be triggered once.
Score bar reflects $mealScore.
*/

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span><span class="round-label">Build a meal</span></div>

<div class="score-bar-wrap">
<span class="score-label">Meal score</span>
<div class="score-bar"><div class="score-bar-fill" @style="'width: ' + Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $mealScore * 1.25)) + '%'"></div></div>
</div>

<div class="content">

<!-- Each ingredient is a plain `<span class="ing-wrap">` with the
     food's emoji / display name / score delta as data-attributes.
     The `:passagedisplay` handler in UserScript wires up TOGGLE
     behaviour on click — earlier this used SugarCube `<<linkreplace>>`
     which is one-way (commits on first tap, no undo) so a player
     who fat-fingered an item couldn't remove it. -->
<div class="section-label">Proteins</div>
<div class="ingredients-grid">
<span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Brown rice" data-ing-emoji="🍚" data-ing-score="10"><span class="ing-emoji">🍚</span><span class="ing-name">Brown rice</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Beans" data-ing-emoji="🍲" data-ing-score="15"><span class="ing-emoji">🍲</span><span class="ing-name">Beans</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Bacon" data-ing-emoji="🥓" data-ing-score="-15" data-ing-diet="meat"><span class="ing-emoji">🥓</span><span class="ing-name">Bacon</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Yogurt" data-ing-emoji="🥛" data-ing-score="10" data-ing-diet="dairy"><span class="ing-emoji">🥛</span><span class="ing-name">Yogurt</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Lentils" data-ing-emoji="🫘" data-ing-score="15" data-ing-diet="plant"><span class="ing-emoji">🫘</span><span class="ing-name">Lentils</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Chickpeas" data-ing-emoji="🫛" data-ing-score="15"><span class="ing-emoji">🫛</span><span class="ing-name">Chickpeas</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Oats" data-ing-emoji="🥣" data-ing-score="10"><span class="ing-emoji">🥣</span><span class="ing-name">Oats</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Grilled chicken" data-ing-emoji="🍗" data-ing-score="5" data-ing-diet="meat"><span class="ing-emoji">🍗</span><span class="ing-name">Grilled chicken</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Salmon" data-ing-emoji="🐟" data-ing-score="10" data-ing-diet="meat"><span class="ing-emoji">🐟</span><span class="ing-name">Salmon</span></span>
</div>

<div class="section-label">Vegetables and Fruit</div>
<div class="ingredients-grid">
<span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Spinach" data-ing-emoji="🥬" data-ing-score="15"><span class="ing-emoji">🥬</span><span class="ing-name">Spinach</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Tomato" data-ing-emoji="🍅" data-ing-score="10"><span class="ing-emoji">🍅</span><span class="ing-name">Tomato</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Banana" data-ing-emoji="🍌" data-ing-score="10"><span class="ing-emoji">🍌</span><span class="ing-name">Banana</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Potato chips" data-ing-emoji="🍟" data-ing-score="-10"><span class="ing-emoji">🍟</span><span class="ing-name">Potato chips</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Broccoli" data-ing-emoji="🥦" data-ing-score="15"><span class="ing-emoji">🥦</span><span class="ing-name">Broccoli</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Avocado" data-ing-emoji="🥑" data-ing-score="10"><span class="ing-emoji">🥑</span><span class="ing-name">Avocado</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Orange" data-ing-emoji="🍊" data-ing-score="10"><span class="ing-emoji">🍊</span><span class="ing-name">Orange</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Pickles" data-ing-emoji="🥒" data-ing-score="-10"><span class="ing-emoji">🥒</span><span class="ing-name">Pickles</span></span>
</div>

<div class="section-label">Extras</div>
<div class="ingredients-grid">
<span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Dark chocolate" data-ing-emoji="🍫" data-ing-score="5"><span class="ing-emoji">🍫</span><span class="ing-name">Dark chocolate</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Instant noodles" data-ing-emoji="🍜" data-ing-score="-20"><span class="ing-emoji">🍜</span><span class="ing-name">Instant noodles</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Water" data-ing-emoji="💧" data-ing-score="5"><span class="ing-emoji">💧</span><span class="ing-name">Water</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Hot dog" data-ing-emoji="🌭" data-ing-score="-15" data-ing-diet="meat"><span class="ing-emoji">🌭</span><span class="ing-name">Hot dog</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Salted crackers" data-ing-emoji="🍘" data-ing-score="-10" data-ing-diet="plant"><span class="ing-emoji">🍘</span><span class="ing-name">Salted crackers</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Nuts" data-ing-emoji="🥜" data-ing-score="10"><span class="ing-emoji">🥜</span><span class="ing-name">Nuts</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Pretzels" data-ing-emoji="🥨" data-ing-score="-15"><span class="ing-emoji">🥨</span><span class="ing-name">Pretzels</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Soda" data-ing-emoji="🥤" data-ing-score="-10"><span class="ing-emoji">🥤</span><span class="ing-name">Soda</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Salt" data-ing-emoji="🧂" data-ing-score="-20"><span class="ing-emoji">🧂</span><span class="ing-name">Salt</span></span>
</div>

<a class="btn-primary" data-passage="Meal Result">SEE MY MEAL RESULT</a>

</div>
</div>

:: Meal Result [Important/Needed nobr] {"position": "1100,100", "size": "100,100"}
/*
MEAL RESULT: Shows what meal does to BP.
Personalized message based on $mealScore.
Lists what player picked.

The <<run>> below fires the canonical SUBMIT_RESPONSE event so
research data sees a DASH Diet play landing in
`surveys/dash_diet_game/responses/{auto}` and a
`survey_response_submitted` event with surveyId='dash_diet_game'.
The Community Stats engagement-bar query keys on the surveyId,
so without this firing the Diet category bar would stay at 0
no matter how many participants finish the game. Guarded by a
session flag so PLAY AGAIN doesn't double-credit.
*/

<<if not $submittedThisSession>>
<<set $submittedThisSession to true>>
<<run
  try {
    if (window.CCQ && typeof window.CCQ.submitResponse === "function") {
      var verdict = "weak";
      if (State.variables.mealScore >= 30) { verdict = "strong"; }
      else if (State.variables.mealScore >= 10) { verdict = "moderate"; }
      else if (State.variables.mealScore >= 0) { verdict = "mixed"; }
      window.CCQ.submitResponse({
        playerName: State.variables.playerName,
        quizScore: State.variables.score,
        quizWrong: State.variables.wrong,
        mealScore: State.variables.mealScore,
        meal: State.variables.meal,
        verdict: verdict
      }, { pointsEarned: 50, countAsCompletion: true });
    }
  } catch (e) { /* swallow */ }
>>
<!-- DAILY GATE: stamp today so Story innit locks the game until tomorrow. -->
<<run try { window.localStorage.setItem("dash_save", JSON.stringify({ dashDate: State.variables.todayDate, pid: State.variables.currentPid })); } catch (e) {} >>
<<set $dashDone to true>>
<</if>>

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span><span class="round-label">Your meal</span></div>

<div class="score-bar-wrap">
<span class="score-label">Meal score</span>
<div class="score-bar"><div class="score-bar-fill" @style="'width: ' + Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $mealScore * 1.25)) + '%'"></div></div>
</div>

<div class="content">

<div class="meal-list-card">
<<if $meal.length gt 0>><div class="meal-emojis"><<for _item range $meal>><<print _item.split(" ")[0]>> <</for>></div><</if>>

<<if $mealScore gte 30>>
<div class="meal-verdict strong">Strong DASH meal</div>
<p class="meal-explain">Your choices are packed with the potassium, fiber, and minerals that help lower blood pressure. Eating meals like this often makes a real difference over a few weeks.</p>
<<elseif $mealScore gte 10>>
<div class="meal-verdict moderate">Good meal</div>
<p class="meal-explain">Some good picks in there. Trading one salty item for a healthy one would move this meal a lot in the right direction.</p>
<<elseif $mealScore gte 0>>
<div class="meal-verdict mixed">Mixed meal</div>
<p class="meal-explain">Your healthy picks are being cancelled out by the salty ones. Small swaps make a real difference here.</p>
<<else>>
<div class="meal-verdict weak">Working against you</div>
<p class="meal-explain">This meal puts pressure on your heart. It has too much salt and not enough potassium. Try replacing one item and see what changes.</p>
<</if>>
</div>

<div class="spacer"></div>

<!-- Single exit button. Direct goHome via the ccq-home-trigger class — the
     bridge intercepts the click and fires CCQ.goHome() to pop the WebView
     route back to the dashboard. -->
<a class="btn-primary ccq-home-trigger" href="javascript:void(0)">BACK TO CARDIOCARE QUEST</a>

</div>
</div>

:: Central Hub [Important/Needed nobr] {"position": "1225,100", "size": "100,100"}
/*
EXIT HATCH. Hit when the player taps "BACK TO CARDIOCAREQUEST" on
either the Final Result or Meal Result screens. Fires CCQ.goHome() so
the Flutter host pops the WebView route back to the dashboard.
Previously had a "PLAY DASH GAME AGAIN" button that just looped back
to Story innit, leaving participants no way to exit.
*/
<<run
  try {
    if (window.CCQ && typeof window.CCQ.goHome === "function") {
      window.CCQ.goHome();
    }
  } catch (e) { /* swallow */ }
>>

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span></div>
<div class="content">

<span class="hero-emoji">🏠</span>

<h2 class="intro-title">Returning</h2>

<p class="narrative center">Going back to CardioCareQuest.</p>

<div class="spacer"></div>

</div>
</div>

:: UserStylesheet [stylesheet]
/* ============================================================
   DASH DIET GAME — visual stylesheet
   Phone-frame UI, viridis dark gradient (purple-blue-teal-green-yellow),
   large emoji food cards. Sister game to Salt Sludge.

   CardioCareQuest viridis palette (canonical across all games):
     #440154  deep purple   — phone gradient stop 1
     #3b528b  blue          — phone gradient stop 2
     #21918c  teal          — phone gradient stop 3 / meter correct
     #5ec962  green          — selected / verdict good (#0a3d12 deep)
     #fde725  yellow         — primary CTA / attention / in-text links
     #f4f1d8  cream          — page background
   ============================================================ */

* { box-sizing: border-box; }

body {
  font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible', system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
  background-color: #f4f1d8;
  margin: 0;
  /* No outer padding: the game fills the screen edge-to-edge on every
     device instead of floating as a card on a cream border. */
  padding: 0;
}

#ui-bar { display: none; }

#story {
  margin: 0 auto;
  /* Fill the full width on phones (was a fixed 380px card, which left
     cream strips on wider screens). */
  max-width: 100%;
  padding: 0;
}

.passage {
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 1em;
  line-height: 1.5;
}

/* Full-screen frame — viridis purple-blue gradient */
.phone {
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #440154 0%, #3b528b 50%, #21918c 100%);
  /* Edge-to-edge: no rounded corners / card shadow now that the gradient
     fills the whole screen. */
  border-radius: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  color: #ffffff;
  position: relative;
  /* Fill the viewport height on every device. dvh tracks the *visible*
     viewport (handles the iOS status/nav bars); vh is the fallback for
     any engine without dvh support. min-height (not height) lets tall
     content still grow and scroll. */
  min-height: 100vh;
  min-height: 100dvh;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 100%;
}

.phone *, .phone *::before, .phone *::after {
  word-wrap: break-word;
  overflow-wrap: break-word;
  max-width: 100%;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

/* Force ALL paragraphs and divs inside .phone to wrap — defends against any
   SugarCube default styles that might force overflow on text content */
.phone p, .phone div {
  word-wrap: break-word !important;
  overflow-wrap: break-word !important;
  white-space: normal !important;
  max-width: 100% !important;
}

/* Header */
.header {
  padding: 16px 22px;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  font-weight: bold;
  color: #ffffff;
  font-size: 16px;
  background-color: rgba(0,0,0,0.25);
  flex: 0 0 auto;
}
.header .round-label {
  opacity: 0.75;
  font-size: 14px;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
}

/* Twin meter section — correct (green) and wrong (purple) */
.meters-wrap {
  padding: 10px 22px 6px 22px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 8px;
}
.meter-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
}
.meter-label {
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  opacity: 0.85;
  width: 72px;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}
.meter-bar {
  flex: 1;
  height: 10px;
  background-color: #ffffff;
  border-radius: 6px;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.meter-bar-fill {
  height: 100%;
  border-radius: 6px;
  transition: width 0.4s ease;
  width: 0%;
}
.meter-bar-fill.correct {
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, #21918c 0%, #5ec962 100%);
}
.meter-bar-fill.wrong {
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, #440154 0%, #3b528b 100%);
}

/* Single score bar for meal builder */
.score-bar-wrap {
  padding: 12px 22px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
}
.score-label {
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  opacity: 0.85;
  width: 80px;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}
.score-bar {
  flex: 1;
  height: 12px;
  background-color: #ffffff;
  border-radius: 6px;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.score-bar-fill {
  height: 100%;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, #21918c 0%, #5ec962 100%);
  border-radius: 6px;
  transition: width 0.4s ease;
  width: 0%;
}

/* Content area */
.content {
  padding: 12px 20px 20px 20px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 100%;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.spacer { flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 6px; }

/* Title for narrative screens */
.intro-title {
  text-align: center;
  font-size: 32px;
  font-weight: normal;
  margin: 0 0 16px 0;
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  word-wrap: break-word !important;
  overflow-wrap: break-word !important;
}

/* Hero emoji */
.hero-emoji {
  font-size: 90px;
  line-height: 1;
  text-align: center;
  display: block;
  margin: 8px auto 16px auto;
}

/* Narrative body */
.narrative {
  font-size: 17px;
  line-height: 1.55;
  margin: 0 0 12px 0;
  text-align: left;
  word-wrap: break-word !important;
  overflow-wrap: break-word !important;
  color: #ffffff !important;
}
.narrative.center { text-align: center; }
.narrative:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 0; }

/* Round Start screen */
.round-status {
  text-align: center;
  font-size: 17px;
  line-height: 1.55;
  margin: 6px 0 14px 0;
  opacity: 0.88;
}

/* Quiz card — single big food in white card */
.quiz-card {
  background-color: #ffffff;
  border-radius: 18px;
  padding: 28px 22px;
  color: #1a1a1a;
  text-align: center;
  margin-bottom: 14px;
  min-height: 240px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 100%;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
.quiz-emoji {
  font-size: 90px;
  line-height: 1;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
  display: block;
}
.quiz-name {
  font-size: 26px;
  font-weight: bold;
  margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  color: #1a1a1a;
}
.quiz-desc {
  font-size: 15px;
  line-height: 1.5;
  color: #555;
  margin: 0;
  word-wrap: break-word !important;
  overflow-wrap: break-word !important;
  white-space: normal !important;
  max-width: 100% !important;
  hyphens: auto;
}

.question-prompt {
  text-align: center;
  font-size: 14px;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  opacity: 0.8;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
}

/* Quiz choice buttons — green for lowers, purple for raises */
.choice-row {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 10px;
}
.choice-btn,
.phone a.choice-btn,
.phone a.choice-btn.macro-link,
.phone a.choice-btn.link-internal {
  display: block !important;
  width: 100% !important;
  padding: 16px 14px !important;
  border-radius: 14px !important;
  font-weight: bold !important;
  font-size: 15px !important;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em !important;
  text-align: center !important;
  text-decoration: none !important;
  font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible', system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif !important;
  cursor: pointer !important;
  border: 2px solid !important;
  box-sizing: border-box !important;
  min-height: 48px !important;
  display: flex !important;
  align-items: center !important;
  justify-content: center !important;
}
.choice-btn.lowers,
.phone a.choice-btn.lowers,
.phone a.choice-btn.lowers.macro-link {
  background-color: #5ec962 !important;
  color: #0a3d12 !important;
  border-color: #5ec962 !important;
}
.choice-btn.raises,
.phone a.choice-btn.raises,
.phone a.choice-btn.raises.macro-link {
  background-color: #440154 !important;
  color: #ffffff !important;
  border-color: #440154 !important;
}

/* Result card on Food Result screen */
.result-card {
  background-color: #ffffff;
  border-radius: 18px;
  padding: 22px 20px;
  color: #1a1a1a;
  text-align: center;
  margin-bottom: 14px;
  min-height: 320px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 100%;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
.result-emoji {
  font-size: 70px;
  line-height: 1;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
  display: block;
}
.result-verdict {
  font-size: 26px;
  font-weight: bold;
  margin: 0 0 14px 0;
}
.result-verdict.correct { color: #21918c; }
.result-verdict.wrong { color: #440154; }
.result-explain {
  font-size: 16px;
  line-height: 1.6;
  color: #444;
  margin: 0;
  word-wrap: break-word !important;
  overflow-wrap: break-word !important;
  white-space: normal !important;
  max-width: 100% !important;
  hyphens: auto;
}

/* Meal builder ingredients */
.section-label {
  font-size: 12px;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  opacity: 0.85;
  margin: 14px 0 8px 0;
  font-weight: bold;
}
.section-label:first-of-type { margin-top: 4px; }

.ingredients-grid {
  display: flex !important;
  flex-direction: row !important;
  flex-wrap: wrap !important;
  width: 100% !important;
  justify-content: flex-start !important;
  align-items: stretch !important;
  margin: 0 -5px !important;
}

/* Each ingredient wrapper is the visible card */
.ingredients-grid .ing-wrap {
  background-color: #ffffff !important;
  color: #1a1a1a !important;
  border: 2px solid transparent !important;
  border-radius: 14px !important;
  padding: 16px 8px !important;
  cursor: pointer !important;
  text-align: center !important;
  font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible', system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif !important;
  display: flex !important;
  flex-direction: column !important;
  align-items: center !important;
  justify-content: center !important;
  min-height: 120px !important;
  width: calc(50% - 10px) !important;
  flex-grow: 0 !important;
  flex-shrink: 0 !important;
  flex-basis: calc(50% - 10px) !important;
  max-width: calc(50% - 10px) !important;
  box-sizing: border-box !important;
  box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1) !important;
  margin: 5px !important;
  text-decoration: none !important;
  transition: all 0.25s ease !important;
}

/* Selected state — added via <<run>> jQuery call when user taps */
.ingredients-grid .ing-wrap.selected {
  background-color: #5ec962 !important;
  border-color: #21918c !important;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(33, 145, 140, 0.35) !important;
}
.ingredients-grid .ing-wrap.selected .ing-name,
.ingredients-grid .ing-wrap .added-name {
  color: #0a3d12 !important;
  font-weight: bold !important;
}
.ingredients-grid .ing-wrap.selected .ing-emoji {
  filter: brightness(1.1);
}

/* Inner linkreplace span — transparent, fills the wrapper */
.ingredients-grid .ing-wrap .macro-linkreplace {
  background-color: transparent !important;
  color: inherit !important;
  border: none !important;
  padding: 0 !important;
  margin: 0 !important;
  box-shadow: none !important;
  display: flex !important;
  flex-direction: column !important;
  align-items: center !important;
  justify-content: center !important;
  width: 100% !important;
  text-decoration: none !important;
}
.ingredients-grid .ing-wrap .macro-linkreplace a {
  color: inherit !important;
  text-decoration: none !important;
  display: flex !important;
  flex-direction: column !important;
  align-items: center !important;
  justify-content: center !important;
  width: 100% !important;
  cursor: pointer !important;
}

/* Fallback for the .added-name text — readable even without .selected */
.added-name {
  color: #0a3d12 !important;
  font-weight: bold !important;
}

.ing-emoji {
  font-size: 50px !important;
  line-height: 1 !important;
  margin-bottom: 8px !important;
  display: block !important;
  text-align: center !important;
  width: 100% !important;
}
.ing-name {
  font-size: 14px !important;
  font-weight: bold !important;
  line-height: 1.2 !important;
  color: #1a1a1a !important;
  display: block !important;
  text-align: center !important;
  width: 100% !important;
}

/* Meal result list */
.meal-list-card {
  background-color: #ffffff;
  border-radius: 18px;
  padding: 20px;
  color: #1a1a1a;
  margin-bottom: 14px;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 100%;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
.meal-list-card .list-title {
  font-size: 13px;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: #888;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
  text-align: center;
}
.meal-list-card .meal-emojis {
  text-align: center;
  font-size: 36px;
  line-height: 1.2;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}
.meal-list-card .meal-verdict {
  font-size: 24px;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-align: center;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}
/* Verdict colors map to viridis stops in their natural order:
   strong = teal (mid viridis), moderate = green (75%), mixed =
   warm-amber semantic-warning (off-palette by design — same
   convention Vascular Village uses for BP stage-1), weak = deep
   purple (low end of viridis, "off the bottom of the scale"). */
.meal-list-card .meal-verdict.strong { color: #21918c; }
.meal-list-card .meal-verdict.moderate { color: #5ec962; }
.meal-list-card .meal-verdict.mixed { color: #f0a020; }
.meal-list-card .meal-verdict.weak { color: #440154; }
.meal-list-card .meal-explain {
  font-size: 15px;
  line-height: 1.55;
  color: #444;
  margin: 0;
  text-align: left;
  word-wrap: break-word !important;
  overflow-wrap: break-word !important;
  white-space: normal !important;
  max-width: 100% !important;
  hyphens: auto;
}

/* Buttons */
.btn-primary,
.phone a.btn-primary,
.phone a.btn-primary.link-internal,
.phone a.btn-primary.macro-link {
  display: block !important;
  width: 100% !important;
  padding: 16px !important;
  background-color: #fde725 !important;
  color: #2a1a4a !important;
  border: none !important;
  border-radius: 14px !important;
  font-weight: bold !important;
  font-size: 16px !important;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em !important;
  text-align: center !important;
  text-decoration: none !important;
  font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible', system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif !important;
  cursor: pointer !important;
  margin-bottom: 10px !important;
  box-sizing: border-box !important;
}
.btn-secondary,
.phone a.btn-secondary,
.phone a.btn-secondary.link-internal,
.phone a.btn-secondary.macro-link {
  display: block !important;
  width: 100% !important;
  padding: 12px !important;
  background-color: transparent !important;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.3) !important;
  color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85) !important;
  border-radius: 14px !important;
  font-size: 13px !important;
  letter-spacing: 0.05em !important;
  text-align: center !important;
  text-decoration: none !important;
  font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible', system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif !important;
  box-sizing: border-box !important;
  min-height: 48px !important;
  display: flex !important;
  align-items: center !important;
  justify-content: center !important;
}

/* Plain in-text links */
.phone a.link-internal:not(.btn-primary):not(.btn-secondary):not(.choice-btn):not(.ingredient):not(.macro-link),
.phone a.macro-link:not(.btn-primary):not(.btn-secondary):not(.choice-btn):not(.ingredient) {
  color: #fde725;
}

:: UserScript [script]
/* twine-user-script #1: "UserScript" */
/* CardioCare Quest — auto passage telemetry.
   Fires `passage_entered` for every passage entry via the FlutterBridge.
   Snapshots SugarCube state.variables so researchers see the player's
   path plus key in-game state. Best-effort; swallows errors. */
$(document).on(":passagestart", function (ev) {
  try {
    if (window.CCQ && typeof window.CCQ.telemetry === "function") {
      var snap = {};
      try { Object.assign(snap, SugarCube.State.variables); } catch (e) {}
      CCQ.telemetry("passage_entered", {
        passage: ev.passage.title,
        vars: snap
      });
    }
  } catch (e) { /* swallow */ }
});


/* DASH Diet Game — Meal Builder ingredient TOGGLE handler.
   Replaces the earlier `<<linkreplace>>` markup which was one-way
   (commit on first tap, no undo). With this handler, every
   `.ing-wrap` is fully toggleable: tap to add → tap again to remove.
   - $meal array is the source of truth for what's been added.
   - $mealScore is recomputed delta-style as items are added/removed.
   - The score bar's width is updated directly (not via SugarCube
     re-render) so the bar moves smoothly inside the same passage.
   - On re-entry to Meal Builder (e.g. via Restart), the handler
     reconstructs the visual state from $meal so previously selected
     items still show as Added.
*/
$(document).on(":passagedisplay", function (ev) {
  if (!ev || !ev.passage || ev.passage.title !== "Meal Builder") return;

  function refreshScoreBar() {
    var fill = document.querySelector(".score-bar-fill");
    if (!fill) return;
    var score = (State.variables && State.variables.mealScore) || 0;
    // Empty-to-full scale, NOT centred around 50%. Sum of all positive
    // ingredient scores is +80 (10+15+15+10+10+10+5+5), so multiply
    // by 1.25 to map a "perfect" meal (+80) to 100% width. Negative
    // ingredients clamp at 0% — bar empties, doesn't drop below.
    // Earlier formula was `score + 50` which painted an empty meal as
    // a half-full bar before the player tapped anything; this is more
    // intuitive ("nothing picked = empty bar").
    var pct = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, score * 1.25));
    fill.style.width = pct + "%";
  }

  function setSelected(wrap, selected) {
    var nameSpan = wrap.querySelector(".ing-name");
    var rawName = wrap.dataset.ingName || "";
    if (selected) {
      wrap.classList.add("selected");
      if (nameSpan) {
        nameSpan.textContent = "✓ Added";
        nameSpan.classList.add("added-name");
      }
    } else {
      wrap.classList.remove("selected");
      if (nameSpan) {
        nameSpan.textContent = rawName;
        nameSpan.classList.remove("added-name");
      }
    }
  }

  // Diet filter: hide meal-builder items the player does not eat, and only
  // show the plant stand-ins (Lentils, Salted crackers) when a diet has
  // removed a meat item, so the "I eat everything" grid stays unchanged.
  var diet = (State.variables && State.variables.playerDiet) || "everything";
  var allWraps = document.querySelectorAll(".ing-wrap");
  for (var w = 0; w < allWraps.length; w++) {
    var wr = allWraps[w];
    var wDiet = wr.dataset.ingDiet || "";
    var hide = false;
    if (wDiet === "meat" && (diet === "vegetarian" || diet === "vegan")) hide = true;
    if (wDiet === "dairy" && diet === "vegan") hide = true;
    // Plant stand-ins only appear for the veg/vegan diets.
    if (wDiet === "plant" && diet === "everything") hide = true;
    // Must use "important" priority: the stylesheet rule
    // `.ingredients-grid .ing-wrap { display: flex !important; }` would
    // otherwise override a plain inline display:none and keep the item visible.
    if (hide) {
      wr.style.setProperty("display", "none", "important");
    } else {
      wr.style.removeProperty("display");
    }
  }

  // Random subset: show only a handful of eligible foods per grid so the
  // menu looks different every play-through. $mealPick is the chosen set,
  // stored so it stays stable while the player is inside this build (e.g.
  // toggling items or navigating away and back). It is reset to null in
  // Story innit and on PLAY AGAIN, so a fresh game re-rolls the choices.
  var SHOW_PER_GRID = 4;
  if (!State.variables.mealPick) {
    var picked = [];
    var grids = document.querySelectorAll(".ingredients-grid");
    for (var g = 0; g < grids.length; g++) {
      var pool = [];
      var kids = grids[g].querySelectorAll(".ing-wrap");
      for (var k = 0; k < kids.length; k++) {
        if (kids[k].style.display === "none") continue; // diet-hidden
        pool.push(kids[k].dataset.ingEmoji + " " + kids[k].dataset.ingName);
      }
      // Fisher-Yates shuffle, then take the first SHOW_PER_GRID.
      for (var s = pool.length - 1; s > 0; s--) {
        var rr = Math.floor(Math.random() * (s + 1));
        var tmp = pool[s]; pool[s] = pool[rr]; pool[rr] = tmp;
      }
      for (var p = 0; p < Math.min(SHOW_PER_GRID, pool.length); p++) {
        picked.push(pool[p]);
      }
    }
    State.variables.mealPick = picked;
  }
  var mealPick = State.variables.mealPick || [];
  var poolWraps = document.querySelectorAll(".ing-wrap");
  for (var pw = 0; pw < poolWraps.length; pw++) {
    if (poolWraps[pw].style.display === "none") continue; // already diet-hidden
    var plbl = poolWraps[pw].dataset.ingEmoji + " " + poolWraps[pw].dataset.ingName;
    if (mealPick.indexOf(plbl) === -1) {
      poolWraps[pw].style.setProperty("display", "none", "important");
    }
  }

  var wraps = document.querySelectorAll(".ing-wrap");
  for (var i = 0; i < wraps.length; i++) {
    var wrap = wraps[i];
    if (wrap.dataset.handlerAttached === "yes") continue;
    wrap.dataset.handlerAttached = "yes";

    var name = wrap.dataset.ingName || "";
    var emoji = wrap.dataset.ingEmoji || "";
    var fullLabel = emoji + " " + name;

    // Restore previously-selected state if the player navigated away
    // and back. Without this every Meal Builder revisit would render
    // unselected even though $meal still contains the items.
    var existingMeal = (State.variables && State.variables.meal) || [];
    if (existingMeal.indexOf(fullLabel) !== -1) {
      setSelected(wrap, true);
    }

    wrap.addEventListener("click", (function (wrap, name, emoji, fullLabel) {
      return function () {
        var scoreDelta = parseInt(wrap.dataset.ingScore || "0", 10);
        var meal = (State.variables.meal || []).slice();
        var idx = meal.indexOf(fullLabel);
        if (idx !== -1) {
          // UNSELECT — remove from $meal, undo score, revert visual.
          meal.splice(idx, 1);
          State.variables.mealScore =
              (State.variables.mealScore || 0) - scoreDelta;
          setSelected(wrap, false);
        } else {
          // SELECT — push to $meal, add score, mark as Added.
          meal.push(fullLabel);
          State.variables.mealScore =
              (State.variables.mealScore || 0) + scoreDelta;
          setSelected(wrap, true);
        }
        State.variables.meal = meal;
        refreshScoreBar();
      };
    })(wrap, name, emoji, fullLabel));
  }
});
/* twine-user-script #2: "DashHelpers" */
/*
DASH Diet Game — food POOL + weighted, non-repeating picker.
Convention: game logic lives here in a [script] passage's setup.*
namespace rather than inline in passages (mirrors Salt Sludge's
SaltHelpers). UPDATE6 (no repeat), UPDATE7 (self-terminating via
null), UPDATE8 (weight the draw toward packaged foods).

setup.dash.foods — every classifiable food. Each object:
  { id, emoji, name, desc, correct: 'lowers'|'raises', explain, packaged }
The emoji / name / desc / correct / explain content for the first six
items is lifted verbatim from the old hardcoded Food Card 1..6 + the
Food Result explain chain; the remaining packaged items were added so
the packaged-weighting actually biases the draw.
*/
setup.dash = setup.dash || {};

setup.dash.foods = [
  {
    id: "banana",
    emoji: "🍌",
    name: "Banana",
    desc: "A common fruit. Sweet. Easy to find. You probably already know someone who eats one every morning.",
    correct: "lowers",
    explain: "Bananas are high in potassium, a mineral that helps your body remove extra salt. Less salt means less pressure on your blood vessels. A banana a day is a real heart-health tool.",
    packaged: false
  },
  {
    id: "noodles",
    emoji: "🍜",
    name: "Instant Noodles",
    desc: "Quick to make. Inexpensive. A meal that shows up in most kitchens at some point.",
    correct: "raises",
    explain: "One packet of instant noodles has about two thirds of all the salt you should eat in a whole day. One packet, before anything else you eat.",
    packaged: true
  },
  {
    id: "darkchocolate",
